Earlier this year we announced that we’d begun concepting a way in which high-level players can challenge themselves with fiendishly tough restrictions on boss fights, and track those challenges in a way they can show off to others.

Known then as PvM Achievement Diaries, we’re extremely excited to announce what is now 'Combat Achievements'.

Combat Achievements is a new system that will complement our current gameplay while offering new challenges for those skilled enough to complete them. As you defeat various bosses throughout Gielinor in dozens of different ways, you’ll also be completing tasks of varying difficulties. Doing so progress through the achievement tiers, and when you’ve done enough of them you’ll find you have access to a whole host of new rewards!

You may even encounter some iconic quest bosses along the way...


{{Horizontal Line}}

{{Headline|22|How exactly do Combat Achievements work?}}

Much like the normal Achievement Diaries, Combat Achievements are split into different tiers of tasks, increasing in difficulty as they progress. There are a lot of bosses and monsters within Old School, so unlike Achievement Diaries' four tiers, Combat Achievements will have six.

[[File:Combat Achievements Poll Blog (1).png|center|500px]]<center>''A WIP image of the Combat Achievements Overview Interface using placeholder graphics. Clicking on the different tiers will automatically filter all tasks. There is also a section showing some of your PvM accomplishments!''</center>


See below for a breakdown of the different tiers and an example of some of the requirements you might expect to be able to fully complete that tier:

''Note: below requirements not intended to be a direct reflection of what is required, they are more of a recommendation for how progressed a typical account may be based on the content you'd likely need to complete.''
*Easy
**Base 60 Combat stats
**50 Slayer
**Dragon Slayer
*Medium
**Base 70 Combat stats
**69 Slayer
**Monkey Madness II
*Hard
**Base 80 Combat stats
**85 Slayer
**Dragon Slayer II
*Elite
**Base 90 Combat stats
**91 Slayer
**Song of the Elves
*Master
**Base 90+ Combat stats
**95 Slayer
**Raiding experience and an understanding of most bosses within the game
*Grandmaster
**Maxed Combat stats
**All previous requirements
**Experienced with all PvM activities within game
**This tier will take our hardest content in the game and push players to their limits. If you thought the Infernal Cape was the difficulty limit, think again!


The additional tiers mean we can be more flexible in our approach with the tasks. Lower tiers are designed to help introduce new and less experienced players into PvM activities, giving them a taste of what combat in the game has to offer. But Master and Grandmaster tiers give us the ability to provide tasks challenging enough to stretch even the most veteran players.


{{Horizontal Line}}

{{Headline|22|Tasks}}

Now that you’ve seen the different tiers available, let’s take a look into what you can expect from the tasks required to complete them.

It’s important we find the right balance between creating tasks that are difficult for groups but also not impossible for solo players. By the same token, we must also avoid creating tasks that are hard to complete solo, yet trivial for groups.

[[File:Combat Achievements Poll Blog (2).png|center|500px]]<center>''A WIP image of the Combat Achievements Tasks interface using placeholder graphics. You can filter tasks by Tier, Type, Monster or their current Completion state. Clicking on a particular task gives more information on what is required for completion.''</center>


Most tasks within Combat Achievements will rely on your ability to complete them alone. There are some exceptions to this, especially when the content itself is designed specifically for groups. Examples include:

*All kill count tasks
**Any previously earnt kill count will carry over and count towards task completions, should Combat Achievements pass the poll.
*Some speed tasks
**Some speed task completions will carry over and count towards task completions, should Combat Achievements pass the poll.
*Most Raids tasks
**There will be tasks for varying group sizes for both Chambers of Xeric and Theatre of Blood
*Most Nightmare of Ashihama tasks


[[File:Combat Achievements Poll Blog (3).png|center|500px]]<center>''A WIP image of the Combat Achievements Boss Overview interface using placeholder graphics. Players can find detailed information about the bosses including requirements to defeat them and their drops. Clicking the 'Map' button opens the world map at the location of the boss, too!''</center>


