{{Headline|22|Rewards}}

Complete all of the tasks within a tier to receive a reward. It wouldn’t be much of an achievement if you were unable to brag about your accomplishments, so let’s take a look at the proposed rewards on offer with Combat Achievements.


''The following rewards would only be obtained once all of the tasks within the relevant tier of Combat Achievements have been completed.''


<center>'''XP Lamps'''</center>


Much like the normal Achievement Diaries, XP lamps are given that scale in experience as you progress through the tiers. These can be used to gain experience in any skill of your choice over a certain level. The following XP lamps would be available:

*Easy Tier - 5k experience in any skill above level 20
*Medium Tier - 10k experience in any skill above level 30
*Hard Tier - 15k experience in any skill above level 40
*Elite Tier - 25k experience in any skill above level 50
*Master Tier - 35k experience in any skill above level 60
*Grandmaster Tier - 50k experience in any skill above level 70

{{News Poll|2|If Combat Achievements are added to the game, should each fully completed tier of tasks reward players with an XP lamp? The amount of experience given would increase as you progress through the different tiers.}}


<center>'''Increased Clue Scroll Drop Rate'''</center>


We propose a 5% increased chance to receive Clue Scrolls you would normally get from drops, with the type of clue changing based on which tier of tasks you had completed. Any skilling or PvM activity would benefit from this increased chance.

''Clue scrolls obtained from Impling Jars or from Clue Caskets would not benefit from this increase.''

*Easy Tier - 5% increased drop chance for Easy Clues
*Medium Tier - 5% increased drop chance for Medium Clues
*Hard Tier - 5% increased drop chance for Hard Clues
*Elite Tier - 5% increased drop chance for Elite Clues

{{News Poll|3|If Combat Achievements are added to the game, should each fully completed tier of tasks give players a 5% increased chance of receiving Clue Scrolls from PvM and Skilling activities as described? Clue scrolls obtained from Impling Jars or from Clue Caskets would not benefit from this increase.}}


<center>'''Like a Boss Upgrade'''</center>


Players who have unlocked the 'Like a Boss' Slayer ability are able to receive boss monster tasks from certain Slayer Masters. The maximum number of boss kills that can be assigned for most tasks is currently 35. As you master the art of boss slaying, each fully completed tier of tasks increases the maximum number of all bosses that can be assigned when 'Like a Boss' is unlocked.

*Easy Tier - +2 to maximum bosses assigned
*Medium Tier - +4 to maximum bosses assigned
*Hard Tier - +6 maximum bosses assigned
*Elite Tier - +8 maximum bosses assigned
*Master Tier - +11 maximum bosses assigned
*Grandmaster Tier - +15 maximum bosses assigned


In addition to the above, we can also extend the number of TzTok-Jad and TzKal-Zuk kills you'd normally be assigned. Failing to defeat either of the bosses would still result in losing the assigned kill, but you'd be able to jump straight back in for another attempt!
*Master Tier - +1 to maximum number of TzTok-Jad and TzKal-Zuk assigned
*Grandmaster Tier - +2 to maximum number of TzTok-Jad and TzKal-Zuk assigned

{{News Poll|4|If Combat Achievements are added to the game, should each fully completed tier of tasks increase the maximum number of all bosses that can be assigned by a Slayer Master when 'Like a Boss' is unlocked?}}
{{News Poll|5|If Combat Achievements are added to the game, should completing all tasks within the Master and Grandmaster tiers increase the maximum number of TzTok-Jad and TzKal-Zuk that can be assigned? Master tier would grant an additional assigned kill, and Grandmaster would grant an additional two assigned kills. Failing to defeat either assigned boss would result in losing one of the assigned kills.}}


