'''Boss Chamber Instances'''

Overcrowding and players crashing one another within God Wars Dungeon has been an increasing problem. There has been a demand to add private instances to the various boss chambers, but there are also concerns over how powerful adding these may be. With Combat Achievements, we feel it's the perfect opportunity to finally be able to offer them, whilst managing the wider impact by locking the instance options behind content that a typical player would complete on their journey to needing them.

While we believe private instances are a great solution to many of the overcrowding problems players face in the God Wars Dungeon, there is still an underlying issue that remains for the majority of Ironmen.

With an ever increasing player base and more players getting their accounts ready to take on the God Wars Dungeon bosses, it can be very difficult for Ironmen to find a free world, especially when they’re ready to start facing off against the likes of General Graardor.

As Ironmen are unable to obtain loot from monsters that have been attacked by other players, they have no opportunity to compete against other players that may want to try and take over their room. This is a common frustration amongst the Ironman community, as it essentially blocks them from being able to complete content they should be able to access.

We feel this can be solved by making it possible for Ironmen to access an Ironman-only version of the individual God Wars Dungeon boss chambers, much as we did for the Corporeal Beast cave. This change would be in addition to the current poll questions regarding private instances, which would be available for all account types.

This change would also mean that Ironmen would only have access to Ironman-only rooms, just as regular accounts only have access to regular rooms. This would still create some competition, but it would be much less troublesome simply because there will be a smaller pool of players to compete with.

In addition, we’d add a ‘Peek’ option to the boss chamber doors for all account types, with a visual effect that lets you quickly identify whether the room is occupied or not and the option to see who’s in there.

The above changes will not be polled, as we feel they are essential for Iron players to experience the content as intended – but we’d like to hear your feedback on the subject.

Upon completion of all tasks within the Hard tier and above, players will gain access to personal instance for the boss chambers with God Wars Dungeon. There is a price to pay for your privacy however, but progressing through the tiers will reduce this slightly. See below for the proposed costs to open a personal God Wars Dungeon instance.

*Hard Tier - 150k coins and the requiured minion kill count
*Elite Tier - 125k coins and the requiured minion kill count
*Master Tier - 100k coins and the requiured minion kill count
*Grandmaster Tier - 75k coins and the requiured minion kill count

Alternatively, players who'd rather skip the required minion kill count can do so by sacrificing an Ecunemical Key alongside some coins.
*Hard Tier - 150k coins and an Ecumenical Key
*Elite Tier - 125k coins and an Ecumenical Key
*Master Tier - 100k coins and an Ecumenical Key
*Grandmaster Tier - 75k coins and an Ecumenical Key

''Note: as the name suggests, personal instances provided by Combat Achievements will be for solo players only.''

{{News Poll|12|If Combat Achievements are added to the game, should completing all tasks within the Hard tier and above give players access to a personal instance for each of the boss chambers within God Wars Dungeon? These instances would cost coins and the required minion kill count, or coins and an Ecumenical Key to enter. These instances would be for solo players only.}}

There are many private instance options throughout Gielinor that require coins in order to access. We'd like to make this more accessible for all players, whilst promoting more opportunities for item sinks. We'd do this by allowing the fee to be taken directly from Death's Coffer, should you have the available funds.

