{{Headline|22|Combat Achievements: A Note on the Future}}

Since we released the blog earlier this week, we've had a fair few comments asking how we're going to approach new content should Combat Achievements pass the poll. While we won't start the full development until it passes, there are some considerations we're already taking into account.
*New bosses and challenges will be added into the respective tiers, but only when they have 'settled' following the update they arrived in. With Old School RuneScape being a living game that is constantly changing based on player feedback, it's highly likely content will be altered slightly after it is released. We'd take this into account before adding any new tasks to Combat Achievements.
*Where we are able to add new tasks with future content releases, we will avoid adding anything that could potentially spoil content. This is especially important to consider with new encounters, as we'd rather not reveal their mechanics until you've had the chance to experience them first!
*We'll be mindful of any changes to content that could make a previously challenging task unintentionally easier.

