{{Headline|22|A New Challenge Approaches}}

It wouldn’t be a true Combat focused update if we weren’t offering you a new challenge to go alongside it, would it? Luckily there are many new challenges included within Combat Achievements that will test your PvM prowess.

While on the topic of new challenges, we'd like to take this opportunity to talk about another combat related update separate from Combat Achievements...

Following a series of failed experiments by the TzHaar, a number of eggs from TzTok-Jad were hatched inside the Inferno. From these eggs came the JalTok-Jads. These creatures are stronger and far more aggressive than TzTok-Jad, and the TzHaar are struggling to deal with them. To help with this, TzHaar-Ket-Rak has challenged any who believe themselves brave enough to enter the Inferno and tackle the JalTok-Jads.

Within the inner city of Mor Ul Rek, players will find TzHaar-Ket-Rak. After a short introduction, he will allow players to take on his challenges. There are six in total, with each seeing the player fight a number of JalTok-Jads. Adventurers must complete the previous challenge to unlock the next. The first two challenges are open to anyone who can access the Mor Ul Rek inner city (unlocked upon showing a Fire Cape to the TzHaar guarding the entrance). The final four challenges require completion of the Inferno.

Much like the Inferno, TzHaar-Ket-Rak's six challenges are considered safe, so players can attempt them without worrying about the effects of death (HCIM rejoice!).

[[File:Combat Achievements Poll Blog (5).png|center|600px]]<center>''A WIP image of the 6-Jad challenge.''</center>


Think you have what it takes to defeat SIX JalTok-Jads at the same time? If you’re successful, you’ll find yourself rewarded with a new JalRek-Jad transmog for the TzRek-Jad pet. You will also receive some Tokkul for each JalTok-Jad killed. The transmog is awarded upon your first completion of the challenge, rather than it being a chance drop. While we did consider the latter, we feel the true replayability value of this challenge is pushing for faster completions.

[[File:Combat Achievements Poll Blog (6).png|center|600px]]<center>''A WIP image of the JalRek-Jad transmog for the TzRek-Jad pet.''</center>


A scoreboard nearby will show personal and global stats for kills, deaths and best times. Who do you think will be the fastest at completing the challenge?

''Note: While we're offering the Six JalTok-Jad Challenge within this blog, it is not dependant upon Combat Achievements. Should both the challenge and Combat Achievements pass in the polls, the Six JalTok-Jad Challenge would be released after Combat Achievements.''

{{News Poll|16|Should TzHaar-Ket-Rak's Six JalTok-Jad Challenge, a new PvM encounter within Mor Ul Rek, be added to the game? Each challenge includes defeating a number of JalTok-Jads, climbing until there are six at the same time. Completing this challenge unlocks a new JalRek-Jad transmog for the TzRek-Jad pet.}}

